Relying on arbitrary sleeps such as `time.Sleep(10 * time.Millisecond)` in asynchronous test routines to coordinate timing can lead to flaky test failures on slower or heavily loaded CI runners. To guarantee deterministic execution, would it be possible to initiate the context cancellation asynchronously within a mock `RoundTripper`? This ensures that the context is canceled precisely when the retry loop transitions to the backoff phase, without requiring arbitrary delays.

```suggestion
		ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
		t.Cleanup(cancel)

		r := newTransportRetryRequest(rtFunc(func(req *http.Request) (*http.Response, error) {
			calls++
			go cancel()
			return nil, fakeTimeoutErr{}
		}))
```

